WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.210
If your prep is MiraLAX, this video will walk you through exactly how to take

2
00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:04.500
it.

3
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.600
Just follow along step by step.

4
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.700
For this prep, you'll need a few items.

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.800
All available over the counter, no prescription needed.

6
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:15.800
You'll need one 238-gram bottle of MiraLAX powder,

7
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.500
two to four Dulcolax laxative tablets,

8
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:23.400
and 64 ounces of a clear sports drink like Gatorade, Propel, or Crystal Light.

9
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.000
That's usually two 32-ounce bottles.

10
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.800
If you have diabetes, use sugar-free Gatorade G2.

11
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.100
Also, make sure you get the laxative tablets, not the stool softener.

12
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:39.500
One important rule, your sports drink cannot be red, orange, blue, or purple.

13
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:42.800
Stick to clear or light-colored flavors.

14
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:46.400
The day before your colonoscopy, you'll start by mixing the solution.

15
00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:50.320
Pour the entire bottle of MiraLAX into a pitcher with all 64 ounces of the

16
00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:51.200
sports drink.

17
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:54.200
Stir or shake until the powder is completely dissolved.

18
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.400
You can chill it in the refrigerator if you'd like.

19
00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.700
Keeping it cold makes it easier to drink.

20
00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:02.300
Now for Part 1. the evening before your procedure.

21
00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:06.000
At 5 p.m., take your Dulcolax tablets with a glass of water.

22
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.600
Your doctor's instructions will tell you whether to take two or four,

23
00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:12.000
follow their guidance on the specific amount.

24
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.300
At 6 p.m., you'll start drinking the first half of the solution.

25
00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.100
That's 32 ounces.

26
00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:21.600
Drink an 8-ounce glass every 15 minutes until that half is gone.

27
00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:24.100
Keep drinking clear liquids after you finish.

28
00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:29.000
For Part 2, six hours before your colonoscopy, you'll drink the second half,

29
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.700
which is another 32 ounces.

30
00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:36.500
Drink this at the same pace: an 8-ounce glass every 15 minutes.

31
00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:41.260
You can continue to have clear liquids up until four hours before your

32
00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:41.800
procedure.

33
00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:43.500
This part is really important.

34
00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:47.300
You must drink all of the prep solution as directed, even if you're already

35
00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.600
passing clear liquid.

36
00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.600
I know it can feel like enough, but finishing the entire dose

37
00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:54.600
is what gives us the clearest view during your procedure.

38
00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:58.600
If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may need to reschedule and neither

39
00:01:58.600 --> 00:01:59.600
of us wants that.

40
00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:03.600
Please drink plenty of liquids throughout the process to prevent dehydration.

41
00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.600
Staying hydrated will help you feel better and help the prep do its job.

42
00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:11.600
If you experience any discomfort from frequent trips to the bathroom,

43
00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:15.600
applying a petroleum-based ointment or diaper rash cream can really help.

44
00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:17.600
That's it. You've got this.

45
00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:21.100
Follow the timing, finish the full dose, and stay hydrated.

46
00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:24.800
If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our office.

47
00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:25.640
We're here to help.
